  "Question": "There are 52 sheets of paper, and 18 are used. How many sheets remain? Calculate: \\(52-18=?\\)",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "34",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "There are not enough ones to subtract. Exchange 1 ten for 10 ones, so 52 becomes 4 tens and 12 ones. Taking away the 18 used sheets leaves \\(12-8=4\\) ones and \\(4-1=3\\) tens. Thus \\(52-18=34\\), so 34 sheets remain.",
